INSERT INTO bio_variants (bio_variant_id, label, usage_context, body_text, sort_order)
VALUES ('fifty-words', 'Fifty words', 'Directory listings, conference programs, deck footers, introductions.', 'David Shadle builds the systems that turn strategy into working software. He is Technical Advisor, Product Strategy and UX at Banyan Software, working across a portfolio of more than 100 B2B SaaS operating companies, where he designed and built the product management platform the program runs on.', 3) ON CONFLICT (bio_variant_id) DO UPDATE SET label = EXCLUDED.label, usage_context = EXCLUDED.usage_context, body_text = EXCLUDED.body_text, sort_order = EXCLUDED.sort_order;

INSERT INTO bio_variants (bio_variant_id, label, usage_context, body_text, sort_order)
VALUES ('one-fifty-words', 'One hundred fifty words', 'Website About block, proposal cover, partner introductions.', 'David Shadle builds the systems that turn strategy into working software. Most advisors stop at the recommendation. He keeps going, through the model, the interface, and the handoff.

He is Technical Advisor, Product Strategy and UX at Banyan Software, working across a portfolio of more than 100 B2B SaaS operating companies. There he designed and built the product management platform the program runs on, and advised on and implemented the experience layer across three executive reporting products covering workshop performance, portfolio operations, and technology due diligence.

He works from a rulebook. The rules of a domain get written down once, in plain language, and the technical pieces are derived from that rather than maintained by hand. It is a working discipline, not a product, and it is what lets him carry a project through delivery rather than stopping at design.

Twenty five years in product strategy and design precede this, including principal roles at Microsoft and Oracle.', 4) ON CONFLICT (bio_variant_id) DO UPDATE SET label = EXCLUDED.label, usage_context = EXCLUDED.usage_context, body_text = EXCLUDED.body_text, sort_order = EXCLUDED.sort_order;

INSERT INTO bio_variants (bio_variant_id, label, usage_context, body_text, sort_order)
VALUES ('three-hundred-words', 'Three hundred words', 'Website Home, long form introductions, anywhere the full argument is wanted.', 'David Shadle builds the systems that turn strategy into working software. Most advisors stop at the recommendation. He keeps going, through the model, the interface, and the handoff, so the thing that gets agreed on is the thing that gets shipped.

He is Technical Advisor, Product Strategy and UX at Banyan Software, working across a portfolio of more than 100 B2B SaaS operating companies, supporting operating company teams, product management, and technology due diligence.

He designed and built the product management platform the program runs on, from concept through production. He advised on and implemented the experience layer across three executive reporting products: workshop maturity and performance, portfolio operations including cloud spend and compliance, and technology due diligence covering deal management and assignment. He rebuilt the Portfolio Operations dashboard onto a database backed foundation, replacing generated exports with live data. With his program team he co-led the redesign of the AI PM Workshop from a training curriculum into an execution engagement, where companies finish with a CEO signed strategy, a prioritized roadmap, and a ledger tracing decisions back to evidence.

His approach starts with the problem. Every engagement begins with a brief that proposes no solution, reviewed by the people who live with the problem, because alignment on the problem is what makes scoping and specification worth doing. From there he works from a rulebook: the rules of a domain written down once in plain language, with the technical pieces derived from that rather than maintained by hand. It is what lets him deliver complete projects rather than stopping at design and project management.

He uses agents as a tool inside the strategy work. Given the context of a specific problem, an agent can research, pressure test a position, and assemble the evidence a decision needs, which surfaces opportunities earlier and builds alignment before execution begins. On a recent engagement with an FDA cleared medical technology company focused on breast cancer prevention, an agent he built acted as domain expert across pilot program design, distribution opportunity, and insurance carrier risk.

Twenty five years in product strategy and design precede this, including principal roles at Microsoft and Oracle. Full stack product practitioner. Not just capable of wearing several hats at once, but confident delivering the outcome in each.', 5) ON CONFLICT (bio_variant_id) DO UPDATE SET label = EXCLUDED.label, usage_context = EXCLUDED.usage_context, body_text = EXCLUDED.body_text, sort_order = EXCLUDED.sort_order;

INSERT INTO bio_variants (bio_variant_id, label, usage_context, body_text, sort_order)
VALUES ('linkedin-about', 'LinkedIn About', 'First person. Roughly two hundred words.', 'I build the systems that turn strategy into working software.

Most advisors stop at the recommendation. I keep going, through the model, the interface, and the handoff, so what gets agreed on is what gets shipped.

I am Technical Advisor, Product Strategy and UX at Banyan Software, working across more than 100 B2B SaaS operating companies. I designed and built the product management platform the program runs on, concept through production. I advised on and implemented the experience layer across our three executive reporting products, and rebuilt the Portfolio Operations dashboard onto live data.

I start with the problem and write it down before anyone proposes a solution. From there I work from a rulebook: the rules of a domain written down once in plain language, with the technical pieces derived from that rather than maintained by hand.

I use agents as a tool inside the strategy work. Given the context of a problem, an agent can research, pressure test a position, and assemble the evidence a decision needs. That surfaces opportunities earlier and builds alignment before execution starts, when alignment is cheap.

It also changed how I think. An agent does exactly what you specify, so vague thinking shows up immediately in the output. You learn to state the job, what a good result looks like, and what the rules are, before anything runs. I do that at the start of strategy work now, long before there is anything to build.

Twenty five years in product strategy and design before this, including principal roles at Microsoft and Oracle.', 6) ON CONFLICT (bio_variant_id) DO UPDATE SET label = EXCLUDED.label, usage_context = EXCLUDED.usage_context, body_text = EXCLUDED.body_text, sort_order = EXCLUDED.sort_order;

INSERT INTO bio_variants (bio_variant_id, label, usage_context, body_text, sort_order)
VALUES ('home-body', 'Home body (first person, no opening paragraph)', 'Website Home, directly under the hero headline/subheadline. Sourced from the Variant A resume''s ''What I do'' paragraphs 2-3 (already first person), which pick up right after the hero''s opening two sentences.', 'I start with the problem and write it down before anyone proposes a solution. From there I work from a rulebook: the rules of a domain written down once in plain language, with the technical pieces derived from that rather than maintained by hand. It is what lets me deliver complete projects rather than stopping at design and project management.

Not just capable of wearing several hats at once, but confident delivering the outcome in each one. Twenty five years in product strategy and design make the systems worth building.', 7) ON CONFLICT (bio_variant_id) DO UPDATE SET label = EXCLUDED.label, usage_context = EXCLUDED.usage_context, body_text = EXCLUDED.body_text, sort_order = EXCLUDED.sort_order;

-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- HowIWorkSections: Table: HowIWorkSections. The method statement for the How I Work page, per David_Shadle_How_I_Work_v1.md. Written to be true indefinitely.
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
INSERT INTO how_i_work_sections (how_i_work_section_id, heading, body_text, short_body_text, sort_order)
VALUES ('problem-first', 'The problem comes first, and it gets its own document', 'Designing against a problem nobody agreed on is the most expensive mistake available. It is also the easiest one to make, because solutions are more interesting to discuss than problems.

So every engagement starts with a brief that contains no screens, no architecture, and no charts. Only the problem, who has it, what it costs, and how we would know it was solved. It gets reviewed by the people who live with the problem before anything else begins.

Doing this properly means real analysis, and the analysis tends to turn things up. On one engagement it surfaced that staging and production were serving two different dashboards. That was a byproduct, not the goal. The goal was an executive team aligned on the problem, which is what makes the scoping and the specification that follow worth doing.', 'Every engagement starts with a brief containing no screens, no architecture, and no charts. Designing against a problem nobody agreed on is the most expensive mistake available.', 1) ON CONFLICT (how_i_work_section_id) DO UPDATE SET heading = EXCLUDED.heading, body_text = EXCLUDED.body_text, short_body_text = EXCLUDED.short_body_text, sort_order = EXCLUDED.sort_order;

INSERT INTO how_i_work_sections (how_i_work_section_id, heading, body_text, short_body_text, sort_order)
VALUES ('model-written-once', 'The model gets written down once', 'Most drift starts small. A chart computes its own version of a metric. The documentation describes last quarter''s schema. Two teams use the same word for different things. Nobody decides to let a system fall out of sync. It happens between decisions.

So I work from a rulebook. The rules of a domain get written down once, in plain language the person who owns the business meaning can read, and the technical pieces are derived from that rather than maintained by hand. Consistency comes from derivation rather than discipline.

What matters here is not the method but what it changed. My responsibility used to end at design and project management, with development handed to someone else. Working this way, I can carry a project from concept through delivery.', 'I work from a rulebook. The rules of a domain get written down in plain language, and the technical pieces are derived from that rather than maintained by hand. Consistency comes from derivation rather than discipline. It is what lets me carry a project through delivery rather than stopping at design.', 2) ON CONFLICT (how_i_work_section_id) DO UPDATE SET heading = EXCLUDED.heading, body_text = EXCLUDED.body_text, short_body_text = EXCLUDED.short_body_text, sort_order = EXCLUDED.sort_order;

INSERT INTO how_i_work_sections (how_i_work_section_id, heading, body_text, short_body_text, sort_order)
VALUES ('no-business-calc-in-interface', 'The interface performs no business calculation', 'Every number on screen traces back to a declared field. A chart that computes its own version of a metric is a defect, not a shortcut.

This sounds like an engineering rule. It is really a trust rule. The moment two surfaces can disagree about the same number, every surface becomes a thing to verify rather than a thing to use.', 'Every number traces back to a declared field. A chart that computes its own version of a metric is a defect.', 3) ON CONFLICT (how_i_work_section_id) DO UPDATE SET heading = EXCLUDED.heading, body_text = EXCLUDED.body_text, short_body_text = EXCLUDED.short_body_text, sort_order = EXCLUDED.sort_order;

INSERT INTO how_i_work_sections (how_i_work_section_id, heading, body_text, short_body_text, sort_order)
VALUES ('prototype-as-alignment', 'It is faster to argue with a wrong sketch than a blank page', 'I build working prototypes early, with real structure and real copy, specifically so people can tell me what is wrong. A prototype is an alignment device, not a deliverable. It exists to be knocked down.

Open questions belong in the room, visible, not resolved quietly and presented as settled. If a review tells me the problem statement was materially wrong, that is the process working, not failing.', 'It is faster to argue with a wrong sketch than a blank page, so I build early and put open questions in the room rather than resolving them quietly.', 4) ON CONFLICT (how_i_work_section_id) DO UPDATE SET heading = EXCLUDED.heading, body_text = EXCLUDED.body_text, short_body_text = EXCLUDED.short_body_text, sort_order = EXCLUDED.sort_order;

INSERT INTO how_i_work_sections (how_i_work_section_id, heading, body_text, short_body_text, sort_order)
VALUES ('named-stages', 'The stages are named, and each one is done when its artifact exists', 'A stage is complete when its artifact exists and its exit criteria are met. Not when the conversation feels finished.

1. Problem brief. The problem, agreed, with no solution in it.
2. Experience design. What it feels like to use, before what it costs to build.
3. Rulebook. The domain written down once, confirmed by the person who owns the meaning.
4. Scope and specification. Every component tied back to something named in the rulebook.
5. Build. Derived where it can be, written where it cannot.
6. Validate and hand off. Tested against the rulebook, handed to a team that owns it.

Not every engagement runs all six. Every engagement runs them in this order.', NULL, 5) ON CONFLICT (how_i_work_section_id) DO UPDATE SET heading = EXCLUDED.heading, body_text = EXCLUDED.body_text, short_body_text = EXCLUDED.short_body_text, sort_order = EXCLUDED.sort_order;

INSERT INTO how_i_work_sections (how_i_work_section_id, heading, body_text, short_body_text, sort_order)
VALUES ('ownership-and-handoff', 'I own the decisions. The team owns the work.', 'I work between executives, operating partners, and delivery teams, and I take ownership of the calls I make. If I set a direction and it turns out to be wrong, that is mine to say and mine to help fix. Putting open questions in the room is not hedging. It is how you get to a decision you can stand behind.

Handing the work back is not stepping away from it. The measure of whether the work was any good is whether it still runs after I am gone. So it gets written in language the people who own it can read, and what gets handed over is whatever that team needs to carry it forward. That is a judgment call each time, not a package.', 'I stand behind the calls I make, and if one is wrong that is mine to say and mine to help fix. Handing the work back is not stepping away. The measure of whether it was any good is whether it still runs after I am gone.', 6) ON CONFLICT (how_i_work_section_id) DO UPDATE SET heading = EXCLUDED.heading, body_text = EXCLUDED.body_text, short_body_text = EXCLUDED.short_body_text, sort_order = EXCLUDED.sort_order;

INSERT INTO how_i_work_sections (how_i_work_section_id, heading, body_text, short_body_text, sort_order)
VALUES ('where-ai-fits', 'Where AI fits', 'I use agents as a tool inside the strategy work, not as an end in themselves.

Given the context of a specific engagement, an agent can do real research, pressure test a position, and assemble the evidence a decision actually needs. That gets me to the problem faster. It surfaces opportunities I would not have found working alone. And it puts something concrete in front of stakeholders early enough to build alignment on the strategy before execution starts, which is when alignment is cheap.

They also changed how I think, which matters more. An agent does exactly what you specify, so vague thinking shows up immediately in the output. You learn to state the job, what a good result looks like, and what the rules are, before anything runs. I do that at the start of strategy work now, long before there is anything to build.', 'Given the context of an engagement, an agent can research, pressure test a position, and assemble evidence. That gets me to the problem faster and builds alignment before execution starts, when alignment is cheap.', 7) ON CONFLICT (how_i_work_section_id) DO UPDATE SET heading = EXCLUDED.heading, body_text = EXCLUDED.body_text, short_body_text = EXCLUDED.short_body_text, sort_order = EXCLUDED.sort_order;

